<h2>Blogroll</h2>

<p class="section-intro">Blogs I read and that inspired this weblog. Old school, long form, people thinking out loud on the internet.</p>

<ul class="link-list">
  <li>
    <a href="https://www.hanselman.com/">Scott Hanselman</a>
    <span class="link-desc">— Scott's been blogging about tech, productivity, and life since 2002. A model for what a developer blog should be.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href="https://blog.codinghorror.com/">Coding Horror</a>
    <span class="link-desc">— Jeff Atwood on programming and human factors. The blog that launched Stack Overflow.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href="https://simonwillison.net/">Simon Willison's Weblog</a>
    <span class="link-desc">— Co-creator of Django. Prolific writer on AI, data, and open source tools. Always interesting.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <a href="https://calnewport.com/blog/">Cal Newport</a>
    <span class="link-desc">— Deep work, slow productivity, and rethinking how we use technology. Changed how I think about focus.</span>
  </li>
</ul>
